A deliberate exception to the repository default of AGPL-3.0-only, for two reasons:

  1. It is a vendored copy of https://github.com/aiosbrain/aios-engineering-harness,
     which is Apache-2.0 upstream. Aligning the licenses keeps the two copies syncable
     in both directions instead of making every sync a licensing question.

  2. `aios repo-bootstrap` copies this directory into a TARGET repository as that repo's
     own `.harness`. A copyleft license here would reach into every repository that
     bootstraps a workspace, which would make the harness unadoptable.

Adopting the harness therefore does not license your repository. Nothing here attaches to
the code it guards, inspects, or generates.

